bootforge/http-rest/rest-and-urls/json-a.instructions:
Export `paginatedResponse(items, page, perPage)` that slices the full `items` array down to the requested page and wraps it:
```
{
  data: [...the page's items...],
  meta: { page, perPage, total, totalPages }
}
```
- `total` is `items.length`; `totalPages` is `Math.ceil(total / perPage)` (0 when total is 0).
- Page 1 starts at index 0; a page beyond the data returns an empty `data` array (meta still correct).

bootforge/http-rest/rest-and-urls/json-a.starter:
export function paginatedResponse(items, page, perPage) {
  // your code here
}

bootforge/http-rest/rest-and-urls/json-a.solution:
export function paginatedResponse(items, page, perPage) {
  const total = items.length;
  const totalPages = Math.ceil(total / perPage);
  const start = (page - 1) * perPage;
  return {
    data: items.slice(start, start + perPage),
    meta: { page, perPage, total, totalPages },
  };
}

